{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian newspaper has issued corrections to several articles published on August 25th. These corrections aim to ensure accuracy and rectify errors in reporting. The corrections span various topics, including crime, business, film, historical relationships, and current events. The paper emphasizes its commitment to providing reliable information and acknowledges the importance of correcting mistakes promptly. Readers are encouraged to be aware of these adjustments for a complete understanding of the original articles. \n\n***\n\nSection 2\nOne correction clarifies the scope of a new pet theft law, stating it applies specifically to England and Northern Ireland, not the entire UK as initially reported. Another addresses a description of Eileen Burbidge, the executive director of Fertifa, correcting her title from \"founder\" to \"executive director,\" while acknowledging the company's actual founders. Additionally, a correction clarifies that the family in the film \"Bend It Like Beckham\" are Sikh, not Muslim, and that Venetia Stanley's uncle, not father, converted to Islam.\n\nSection 3\n* The article regarding the new pet theft law incorrectly stated the legislation applied to the entire UK. The correction clarifies it applies only to England and Northern Ireland.\n* The reporting on Eileen Burbidge's role at Fertifa mistakenly referred to her as the \"founder\" instead of the \"executive director.\"\n\nSection 4\nThe Observer, the newspaper's sister publication, has also published a list of recently amended articles, covering a wide range of subjects from international affairs to cultural exhibitions. Readers can find the original articles and the corrections listed above on The Guardian's website or in the print edition. The paper provides multiple ways for readers to contact the Readers’ Editor to provide feedback or report any further inaccuracies.\n\nWrite to the Readers’ Editor, the Observer, York Way, London N1 9GU, email observer.readers@observer.co.uk, tel 020 3353 4736\n\nP.P.S. The corrections highlight the importance of meticulous fact-checking in journalism and the ongoing efforts of news organizations to maintain accuracy and credibility.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -0.00033802041434682906}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.3870837688446045}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.0902138277888298}, {"token": "▁Guardian", "logprob": -0.011430961079895496}, {"token": "▁newspaper", "logprob": -0.35608676075935364}, {"token": "▁has", "logprob": -0.030237458646297455}, {"token": "▁issued", "logprob": -0.056602247059345245}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.6817901134490967}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.008365116082131863}, {"token": "▁several", "logprob": -0.00014530557382386178}, {"token": "▁articles", "logprob": -0.05526195093989372}, {"token": "▁published", "logprob": -2.2053474822314456e-05}, {"token": "▁on", "logprob": -0.0005721600609831512}, {"token": "▁August", "logprob": -9.274052717955783e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -3.4570634852570947e-06}, {"token": "th", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.011111760511994362}, {"token": "▁These", "logprob": -0.011743108741939068}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.12817256152629852}, {"token": "▁aim", "logprob": -1.653472661972046}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -1.156323378381785e-05}, {"token": "▁ensure", "logprob": -0.11440121382474899}, {"token": "▁accuracy", "logprob": -0.04688538610935211}, {"token": "▁and", "logprob": -0.005354586523026228}, {"token": "▁rectify", "logprob": -1.5110740661621094}, {"token": "▁errors", "logprob": -0.3004700243473053}, {"token": "▁in", "